<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguayan reserves fall 11.7 pct to $977 mln.</title>
<headline>Paraguayan reserves fall 11.7 pct to $977 mln.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay's foreign currency reserves have fallen 11.7 percent over the 12 months to $977 million from $1.1 billion at the end of last year, the Central Bank said Friday.</p>
<p>Official sources said reserves fell due to foreign debt payments and Central Bank spending to bolster the local gauarani currency during the first quarter of the year.</p>
<p>Reserves were $1.0 billion in December 1994.</p>
<p>((-Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom, 595 21 444527))</p>
